  "body": "Maintainer request from #1452 (\"We should be able to load DXF file to do profile cuts on.\").\n\nDepends on #1864.\n\n## Goal\nExtend `Slot` and `TrochoidalSlot` beyond two-point parameters so operations consume DXF sketch centerlines and closed slot profiles.\n\n## Scope\n- Update `OpParams::Slot` and `OpParams::TrochoidalSlot` (`crates/app/src/operation/types/params.rs`, `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`) to accept `SrcRef::Selection` DXF sketch chains or layers alongside legacy `a`/`b`/`width` parameters (keeping existing `.camproj` files compatible).\n- Support two sketch slot inputs cleanly:\n  1. Open or closed centerline chains (`Line`, `Arc`, `Polyline`) milled to a configured slot `width` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/slots.rs`).\n  2. Closed stadium or line-arc slot loops where width derives from the boundary or fits within tool diameter limits.\n- Refuse channels narrower than tool diameter, open chains with invalid geometry, or non-slot outlines with named diagnostics.\n- Transform paths by sketch `Location` and setup alignment and verify/simulate against setup stock cleanly (`part_solid = false`).\n\n## Done means\n`Slot` and `TrochoidalSlot` generate size-accurate passes and golden CL from DXF line-arc slot sketches without typing manual endpoints; invalid slot widths fail by name; existing `.camproj` two-point slot tests continue to pass.\n\nPart of #1452\n",
